    "sections": [
      {
        "section_id": "S01",
        "title": "Permission intersection",
        "text": "Check tool, model version, deployment, purpose, data classes, user population and case conditions together. All must permit the activity. Model approval alone never approves an endpoint. No approved deployment permits raw personal data or Restricted information."
      },
      {
        "section_id": "S02",
        "title": "Status semantics",
        "text": "Approved means only the recorded scope. Pilot only means named pilot participants and pilot purposes, not production. Under review, Blocked, Revoked and unlisted combinations do not permit company use. Expired case authorization cannot be rescued by an Approved catalog status."
      },
      {
        "section_id": "S03",
        "title": "Configuration and freshness",
        "text": "Snapshot is 2026-11-08T00:00:00Z. Owner-approved changes produce a new catalog version. Preserve historical snapshots for decisions. All names, providers, settings and .example endpoints in this catalog are fictional; they do not describe real vendor behavior."
      }
    ]
  },
